---
// ABOUT — what PIL.AGRIGEA is: the box, the iceberg, the tree, the skool.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { TAGLINES } from '../data/ontology'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — PIL.AGRIGEA"
  description="What PIL.AGRIGEA is — the box, the iceberg, the tree, and the skool of fishes."
>
  <article class="container prose" style="padding-top: var(--space-7); padding-bottom: var(--space-7);">
    <p class="section__label"><a href="/">← Deck</a></p>

    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      PIL.AGRIGEA is a public lab for turning observed chaos into tested
      hypotheses. One box to stand in, one iceberg to descend, one tree of
      pills to swallow, one school of fish to argue with.
    </p>

    <h2>The box</h2>
    <p>
      {TAGLINES.observation} The observation deck is the only place this site
      claims you should stand. Everything below is inference.
    </p>

    <h2>The iceberg</h2>
    <p>
      The iceberg is an <strong>inference engine</strong>: 10% observable, 90%
      inferred. Five layers descend from the surface toward the paradigm —
      <span class="mono">MATRIX → FRAMES → PILLS → DEEP → SOURCE</span>. Each
      layer observes, detects, infers, validates, or reveals. Nothing below the
      waterline is a fact; it is a working model.
    </p>

    <h2>The tree</h2>
    <p>
      {TAGLINES.pharmacology} The tree is the <strong>pharmacology of the
      pills</strong>: roots to trunk to branches to fruits, five pills —
      blue, red, black, white, grey — that oppose, complement, and cure each
      other. Ideas are dosed, not believed.
    </p>

    <h2>The skool</h2>
    <p>
      The skool of fishes is the <strong>living record</strong>: a network of
      posts, each a structured fishbone swimming through the iceberg at a
      depth, tinted by a pill, carried by a current. The skool is never
      complete. It grows by pull request, argues by discussion, and changes
      its mind in public.
    </p>

    <h2>The stack</h2>
    <p class="mono">
      ASTRO 5 · REACT ISLANDS · TYPESCRIPT · STATIC HTML OUTPUT · ZERO RUNTIME
      DEPENDENCIES · CLOUDFLARE PAGES
    </p>
    <p>
      The site compiles to flat, static HTML at build time. The interactive
      network and the tree explorer are small client-side islands; everything
      else is plain markup. There is no server, no database, no tracking.
      {TAGLINES.ethos}
    </p>

    <h2>Identity</h2>
    <p>
      Signed <span class="mono">Pil_aG</span> — the ghost in the box. The
      methodology is self-hosted and dependency-free, which is itself one of
      the pills this site swallows.
    </p>

    <div class="divider"></div>
    <p class="mono faint">WE ARE COOKING KNOWLEDGE.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
